  "findings": [
    "Public programme order selects High-tech Designer Materials first, independently of UCR fit. The guide API orders its dropdown differently; that display order does not overturn the original public tie-break. The track is ten individual units totalling 54 EC, not 54 additional credits on top of those units. API year-two total 168 sums three mutually exclusive tracks plus the common project and is not a valid single-student total. One selected track plus Design Project is sixty credits.",
    "The introductory programme describes interdisciplinary natural science, modelling, design, experiments and tangible prototypes. Makerspace activity is central, not an incidental example. The first year includes mechanics/materials, light, biochemistry, energy, digital work and skills. Individual dated catalogue entries confirm component credit values.",
    "Quantum Physics 1 is explicitly in the materials track, but the course entryRequirements lists only Physics/Astronomy and Bèta-gamma Physics. The course recommended knowledge separately permits other backgrounds if they have mathematics and physical optics; this recommendation does not itself remove the formal entry restriction. Do not infer an access exception.",
    "Design Project is mandatory across all tracks, includes preparatory workshops throughout the year and implementation in period six. Advanced Ethical Prototyping requires first year completed, 120 EC and Design Project; it is a full-time eight-week physical prototype with explicit ethical decisions, measurement, demonstration and defence. Bachelor Project has the same entry thresholds, independent supervised research, thesis/presentation and at least two UvA examiners. External projects require Board permission.",
    "Thirty genuinely open credits normally occupy semester one of year three. At most twelve may be first-year subjects, content may not duplicate compulsory work and the Board assesses the study plan; foreign minors need prior approval. No package or host is invented."
  ],
  "unresolved": [
